# W44-87 single-pass-entropy dispatch A/B
# date: 2026-05-19
# runs_per_cell: 3
# images: 5 CID22 validation photos (512x512)
#   1025469 1044329 1189261 1418519 1531677
# effort: e5
# distances: d=1.0
# modes:
#   baseline:  SinglePassEntropyDispatch::AlwaysTwoPass (default)
#   auto:      SinglePassEntropyDispatch::Auto (gated on effort==5, distance<=1.0, median<50, safety)
#   forced:    SinglePassEntropyDispatch::AlwaysSinglePass (worst case, ignores content)
#
# Summary (medians of 3 runs):
#   image      mask1x1  base_B  base_ms   auto_B/Δ%  auto_ms  forced_B/Δ%  forced_ms
#   1025469      76     37823    523        0.0%      520       +34.8%       16
#   1044329      48     99865    734       +16.0%      19       +16.0%       17     <- dispatch fires
#   1189261      69     64770    671        0.0%      700       +13.4%       19
#   1418519      92     21186    512        0.0%      508       +27.6%       19
#   1531677      36     82765    421       +14.3%      19       +14.3%       19     <- dispatch fires
#
# Findings:
#   - Wall-clock saving is real and large (~400-730 ms per 512x512 encode at e5 d=1.0)
#     when the dispatch fires (>>5ms gate from task spec, way more than W38 prediction of 7-14ms).
#   - BUT byte regression is +13-35% — far above the +5% acceptance threshold.
#     W38 memo predicted -2 to -4% bytes on smooth photos at d<=1.0; the actual regression
#     is 5-7x worse. Static codes are tuned for an averaged token distribution that doesn't
#     fit any single image as tightly as per-image-optimized codes, and the smooth-photo
#     class isn't homogeneous enough to share a single optimal code.
#   - Default `AlwaysTwoPass` keeps every hash-lock byte-identical (36/36 hash-lock tests
#     pass; 1258 lib tests pass).
#   - Multi-decoder roundtrip OK on a dispatched output (1044329):
#       jxl-oxide: parsed + rendered cleanly
#       djxl 0.12.0: decoded cleanly (32 threads, 66.5 MP/s)
#       jxl-rs (CLI): decoded to PNG cleanly
#
# Conclusion: ship the dispatch INFRASTRUCTURE (enum + builder + plumbing) as opt-in,
# default-off. Caller can pin `AlwaysSinglePass` for offline pipelines that want the
# wall-clock saving and accept the byte cost. Default flip to `Auto` is NOT recommended
# without (a) a wider corpus bench (b) a per-image classifier sharper than mask1x1
# median or (c) hybrid codes that bake in per-class distributions.
#
# Reproducer:
#   cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features parallel \
#     --example w44_87_single_pass_ab -- --runs 3 \
#     --out benchmarks/single_pass_entropy_dispatch_2026-05-19.tsv
